# {{.Title}}'s features: what each is, the routes it's made of, who it's for,
# and the pages to check it by. TestFeatures (app/features_test.go) fails on a
# route that's in none, and bin/gantry verify visits each feature's pages as
# each role.
#
#   routes:    as bin/gantry routes lists them: "GET /posts", or "/posts" for
#              any method; one ending in / is every route under it too
#              ("/posts/"). Mounted routes (files, the development inbox)
#              needn't be in one.
#   role:      who it's for: public, signed-in or admin.
#   cacheable: its routes are Cached, and its pages are the same for everyone
#              its role lets in.
#   visit:     pages to request: a path, the status it answers (200 if not
#              given) and a CSS selector for an element the page has.
#
# g resource and g auth add theirs. The guide:
# https://github.com/scttymn/gantry/blob/{{.Gantry}}/docs/development.md#the-feature-map
features:
  - name: home
    routes:
      - GET /{$}
    role: public
    visit:
      - path: /
        selector: h1
  - name: health check
    routes:
      - GET /up
    role: public
    visit:
      - path: /up
  - name: live updates
    routes:
      - GET /live
    role: public
